# /etc/cron.d/cinesets  (times use this machine's time zone: check with `timedatectl`)
# CineSets by blurbery (https://github.com/blurbery/cinesets). SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
# Additional terms under AGPL-3.0 section 7 apply: see NOTICE.
# Every 6 hours: Trending Top 20. Daily at 04:30: charts and seasonal. Sundays at 05:00: everything.
# CineSets also takes its own lock, so overlapping runs wait for each other.
#
# Replace YOUR-USER with the user that owns /opt/cinesets (ls -ld /opt/cinesets shows it), and the paths if yours
# differ. Use root only if root owns the folder: CineSets won't run as root in a folder that belongs to someone else,
# because root's files there would stop that user's own runs.
0 */6 * * * YOUR-USER /opt/cinesets/run.sh apply --only m-trending,s-trending > /opt/cinesets/logs/trending.log 2>&1
30 4 * * * YOUR-USER /opt/cinesets/run.sh apply --group seasonal,charts > /opt/cinesets/logs/daily.log 2>&1
0 5 * * 0 YOUR-USER /opt/cinesets/run.sh apply > /opt/cinesets/logs/weekly.log 2>&1
